ANGULAR NOTES – FUNDAMENTALS (v1 → v2+)
======================================

--------------------------------------------------
1. Node.js
--------------------------------------------------

Node.js:
• Runtime environment for executing JavaScript
• Allows JavaScript to run outside the browser
• Mandatory for Angular development

Check Node version:
node --version
(or)
node -v


--------------------------------------------------
2. Angular Overview
--------------------------------------------------

Angular:
• A front-end framework built on top of Node.js ecosystem
• Uses TypeScript
• Used for building Single Page Applications (SPA)

Note:
• AngularJS (v1) is different from Angular (v2+)
• Angular v2+ is a complete rewrite and not backward compatible


--------------------------------------------------
3. Installing Angular CLI
--------------------------------------------------

Install Angular CLI globally:
npm install -g @angular/cli

Check Angular CLI version:
ng --version

Angular CLI is used to:
• Create projects
• Generate components, services, modules
• Build and serve applications


--------------------------------------------------
4. Node Modules
--------------------------------------------------

node_modules:
• Contains all third-party libraries
• Installed using npm
• Not deployed to production
• Can be regenerated using package.json

Command to install dependencies:
npm install


--------------------------------------------------
5. Angular Project Structure
--------------------------------------------------

src/
• Contains complete source code of the application

src/app/
• Contains components and modules
• Core business logic lives here

src/assets/
• Images, fonts, static files

src/environments/
• Configuration files for different environments
• Example: dev, production

main.ts:
• Entry point of the Angular application
• Bootstraps the root module

polyfills.ts:
• Imports JavaScript libraries needed for browser compatibility
• Ensures Angular works in older browsers


--------------------------------------------------
6. Configuration Files
--------------------------------------------------

angular.json:
• Main Angular configuration file
• Build, serve, assets, styles configuration

karma.conf.js:
• Configuration file for unit testing

package.json:
• Lists project dependencies
• npm scripts
• Application metadata

tsconfig.json:
• TypeScript compiler configuration
• Controls transpilation rules


--------------------------------------------------
7. Build Process
--------------------------------------------------

• All TypeScript files are compiled into JavaScript
• Output is bundled into optimized JS files
• Bundles are deployed to the server/browser


--------------------------------------------------
8. Angular v2+ Essentials
--------------------------------------------------

TypeScript:
• Superset of JavaScript
• Adds static typing
• Improves maintainability and tooling

Typing:
• Optional but recommended
• Helps catch errors at compile time

Transpilation:
• TypeScript compiler converts TS → JS

Command:
tsc main.ts


--------------------------------------------------
9. Variables in TypeScript
--------------------------------------------------

Using var:
var count = 4;
• Function scoped
• Avoided in modern TypeScript

Using let:
let count = 3;
• Block scoped
• Similar to C# variable scope

Type Safety:
• Once a type is assigned, it cannot change

Example:
let count: number;
count = 10;      // valid
count = "ten";   // error

Without type:
let value;
• Type is any
• Can change to any data type


--------------------------------------------------
10. Arrow Functions
--------------------------------------------------

Arrow Functions:
• Equivalent to C# lambda expressions
• Shorter syntax for functions

Example:
let doLog = (message) => console.log(message);

Or:
let doLog = (message) => {
  console.log(message);
};


--------------------------------------------------
11. Access Modifiers in TypeScript
--------------------------------------------------

public:
• Accessible everywhere (default)

private:
• Accessible only within the class

protected:
• Accessible within class and derived classes


--------------------------------------------------
12. Angular Building Blocks
--------------------------------------------------

Component:
• Heart of every Angular application
• Controls a part of the UI
• Example: Navbar component

Component encapsulates:
• Data
• HTML Template
• Logic

Module:
• Container for a group of related components
• Organizes application into logical units


--------------------------------------------------
13. Creating a Component (Flow)
--------------------------------------------------

Steps:
1. Create a component
2. Register it in a module
3. Add the selector in HTML

CLI Command:
ng generate component component-name
(or)
ng g c component-name

Usage in HTML:
<app-component-name></app-component-name>
